From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Er Gibbio <gibbio@pm.me>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:00:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/21] vt: show pictures up to 15 ms late instead of dropping
 them

On the Proxmox node's H.264 streams (Quick Sync), the VideoToolbox decoder
dropped a picture every 2-3 s, each 1-9 ms past its time: decoded just after
it on a busy main context. Dropping one holds the previous picture for
another frame period, a visible stutter, where showing it a few ms late is
not. Pictures later than that are still dropped.
---
 src/channel-display-vt.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/channel-display-vt.c b/src/channel-display-vt.c
index 44d75f9..360c104 100644
--- a/src/channel-display-vt.c
+++ b/src/channel-display-vt.c
@@ -23,7 +23,8 @@
  * hardware decode takes a few milliseconds, the builtin MJPEG decoder decodes
  * inline the same way — and every frame is decoded, since later frames reference
  * earlier ones. Pictures come out as BGRA (converted by VideoToolbox) and wait in a
- * queue for their multimedia time; late ones are dropped at display time only.
+ * queue for their multimedia time; ones more than VT_LATE_TOLERANCE_MS late are
+ * dropped at display time only.
  */
 #include "config.h"
 
@@ -34,6 +35,12 @@
 #include "spice-channel-priv.h"
 #include "channel-display-priv.h"
 
+/* A picture this late is still shown, at once. The pictures dropped as late
+ * were 1-9 ms past their time (decoded just after it on a busy main context),
+ * and dropping one holds the previous picture on screen for another frame
+ * period, 33 ms at 30 fps: a visible stutter where a few ms late is not. */
+#define VT_LATE_TOLERANCE_MS 15
+
 typedef struct VTPicture {
     SpiceFrame *frame;          /* mm_time and destination of the picture */
     CVPixelBufferRef image;     /* decoded BGRA picture */
@@ -393,9 +400,10 @@ static void vt_decoder_schedule(VTDecoder *decoder)
     decoder->cur = NULL;
     do {
         if (picture != NULL) {
-            if (spice_mmtime_diff(time, picture->frame->mm_time) <= 0) {
+            gint32 late = spice_mmtime_diff(time, picture->frame->mm_time);
+            if (late <= VT_LATE_TOLERANCE_MS) {
                 decoder->cur = picture;
-                decoder->timer_id = g_spice_timeout_add(picture->frame->mm_time - time,
+                decoder->timer_id = g_spice_timeout_add(late < 0 ? -late : 0,
                                                         vt_decoder_display_picture, decoder);
                 break;
             }
